+# Issue #25 closeout — BLOCKED
+
+Product source is frozen at `105cd7ef5b47e194be1fbfd2271ba6d96c0fd32f`, base `8b6321276f33923f24f15a8437205b6126bf92ca`. This directory is an evidence-only closeout, not a product fix or a PASS for a subsequent evidence commit. PR #26 remains Draft; issue #25 remains open and blocked. No merge was attempted.
+
+The user supplied the included timeout screenshot. The associated earlier freeze6 human attempt reached ready/listening, then timed out without a final result. It is a failed recognition observation, not a success. Freeze7 changes microphone ownership to foreground app AudioRecord, keeps bounded PCM in memory, and submits it to the vehicle-local Pleos ON_DEVICE service. User permission for Mac input and Android microphone while using the app was explicitly granted in chat. Android permission was actually granted on B through its OS UI; A's app permission remains ungranted.
+
+The latest installed freeze7 B test used synthesized speech played through the Mac speaker into the actual app microphone. It was neither human speech nor supplied-PCM injection. `runtime/f7-app-record-to-engine-B.json` records appMicrophoneRecording, appMicrophoneClosed and sdkPcmCompleted, followed by failureTIMEOUT; finalReceived is false. Microphone capture followed by service submission therefore does not establish transcription success. The cause of missing final recognition remains unresolved. Earlier public-PCM driver success belongs to a different path and is not reused as this APK's runtime PASS.
+
+The independent verifier inspected exact source HEAD and reran core93/app105 = 198 JVM tests and Node94 tests, all passing, plus app/driver assemble and lint (errors0; warnings13/8). Its already-running Gradle completed after the run deadline; the original report and dated addendum preserve this distinction. APK full hashes differ between independent and builder packaging, while all decompressed payload entries match (app886, driver883). See verifier/build-result.json, apk-payload-comparison.json and verification-review.md. Overall remains BLOCKED; static checks cannot replace device evidence.
+
+Missing required evidence includes successful latest human microphone recognition, latest cancellation/foreground exit/retry behavior on both cars, actual edited draft and saved-place candidates, fontScale1.3 and long text, and current two-car receipt/rejection/pending route0/unanimous acceptance followed by real native confirmation. No current two-car proposal was completed. No prior route observation is reused as this run's continuity proof; recovery and collector gaps remain gaps.
+
+Only dedicated ADB5041, emulator-5570/Pleos12Leader and emulator-5572/Pleos12Follower, user10 were operated. The old4190 server and original checkout were preserved; this run used separate loopback4192 and a task room. Same AVD data was preserved during A recovery; no wipe or snapshot restore occurred. The original846 evidence blobs were independently checked unchanged. Excluded phone issues #7/#8 and map issue #16 were not implemented.
+
+The repository harness limits one bundle to120minutes from2026-11-08T10:13:20Z (deadline12:13:20Z), without resetting on resume. Product changes and new tests stopped at closeout; remaining actions only preserve evidence and publish truthful blocked status. The final read-only app-op check shows no active recording on either app. B's approved host microphone input remains enabled for the pending optional user retest; Android permission and host input state are distinct. No user recording, encrypted session blob, invitation, credential, APK or generated audio fixture is included in this directory. Raw logs preserve their original whitespace.
+
+Further implementation requires an explicitly scoped new execution bundle; it must not reset this bundle's elapsed-time record. Before any merge, rerun the mandatory device scenarios and obtain independent PASS against the exact final base/head. The unfinished task is not represented as complete.
